WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.710
Follow the ovary and the uterine lining together.

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:07.000
Rising follicle-stimulating hormone
stimulates follicular growth.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.956
One follicle becomes dominant
and produces increasing estradiol.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.038
Estrogen drives proliferation of the endometrium.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.082
The luteinizing hormone surge causes ovulation.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.045
Watch the mature follicle release the ovum.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.240
Then follow the remaining follicle as it becomes the

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.160
corpus luteum.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.577
Luteinizing hormone stimulates the
corpus luteum to secrete progesterone.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.608
Progesterone initiates the secretory phase.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.980
Endometrial glands and blood
vessels branch and curl through

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:35.832
the functional layer.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.869
If implantation does not
occur, the corpus luteum degenerates.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:44.180
Estrogen and progesterone fall,
and the endometrium degenerates and

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:44.560
sheds.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:48.657
The hormone sequence explains
the tissue sequence: follicular growth,

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:51.902
ovulation, secretory change, and menstruation.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:56.591
Estrogen supports proliferation;
progesterone initiates secretion.
